.\" Manpage for puravida.
.TH PURAVIDA 1 "2026-06-11" "puravida 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puravida \- create files and directories in one command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puravida
.I path
.br
.B puravida
.I dir file ...
.br
.B puravida
.I file content ...
.br
.B puravida
.I file
.B ~
.br
.B puravida \-\-help
.br
.B puravida \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puravida
is a one\-liner replacement for
.BR mkdir (1)
and
.BR touch (1),
and a cleaner alternative to here\-documents for writing text into a file.
Parent directories are created as needed.
.PP
Whether an argument is treated as a file or a directory is decided by its final
path segment: if that segment contains a period (for example
.IR notes.txt )
it is treated as a file; otherwise it is treated as a directory. A period in a
parent segment is fine, so
.I my.dir/notes
still creates
.I my.dir
as a directory.
.PP
For inline contents, quoting is handled by your shell: double quotes expand
variables while single quotes keep everything literal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B puravida src/utils/helpers.js
Create the nested directories and an empty file.
.TP
.B puravida src index.tsx styles.css
Create the directory
.I src
containing two empty files.
.TP
.B puravida notes.txt "hello there"
Create
.I notes.txt
containing the text
.IR "hello there" .
.TP
.B puravida notes.txt ~
Create
.I notes.txt
from pasted input; finish by entering a line containing only
.BR ~ .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error (for example, a file or directory could not be created).
.TP
.B 2
A usage error (no arguments, or an unknown option).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR touch (1)
